WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.290
Pack, price and sell your soap without losing money.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:08.440
This is the video for Module 4: packaging, costing and selling your soap.

3
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:14.340
A good bar only becomes income when it is packed well and labelled honestly.

4
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:20.120
When it is priced from your real costs, not from oil and caustic soda alone.

5
00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:24.030
And when it is sold to customers who come back.

6
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:40.790
Check every label against this list. Product name. Ingredients, from largest to smallest. Net weight, set below your tested dried weight. Your name and phone number. Batch code and date. And cautions, such as keep out of reach of children.

7
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.280
Print a NAFDAC number only once you have been given one.

8
00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:58.370
A batch code links every bar to its batch sheet. Take LB-2610-07. LB means laundry bar. BB is bath bar and LP is laundry powder.

9
00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:04.640
2610 means the year 2026, month 10.

10
00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:15.060
And 07 is the seventh batch that month. If a customer complains, you find the date, the oil supplier and the test results in minutes.

11
00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:25.290
Never wrap bars before drying or curing is complete and the batch has passed its tests. Wet soap can sweat or spot inside the wrapper.

12
00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:41.240
Many soap makers count only oil and caustic soda, then wonder why no money is left. For example, Chinyere costs her 10 kg-oil laundry run from Module 2. Her prices are examples; use your own receipts.

13
00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:47.500
She lists the PKO, palm oil, caustic soda, clean water and gas for the cook.

14
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.890
Then 73 wrappers and labels.

15
00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:58.540
Then labour, 2 helpers at 3,000 naira each. Count your own time too, even if you work alone.

16
00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:02.470
And a fair share of rent, transport and phone.

17
00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:15.120
Her total is 42,540 naira. Divided by 73 good bars, that is 583 naira per bar. Any price below that loses money.

18
00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:29.080
Now she sets prices. Wholesale is 750 naira, a profit of 167 naira per bar. Retail is 900 naira, a profit of 317 naira.

19
00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.280
48 bars sold wholesale bring 36,000 naira.

20
00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:40.130
25 bars sold retail bring 22,500 naira.

21
00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:54.720
Total sales are 58,500 naira. Take away the 42,540 naira cost, and she earns 15,960 naira profit, after paying her helpers.

22
00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:58.550
If PKO rises, she reruns the cost sheet at once.

23
00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:09.250
Laundry soap is used up every week, so it brings repeat orders. Market traders and kiosks want cartons of laundry bars at a wholesale price.

24
00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:19.970
Laundries, schools and hostels want bulk bars and powder, delivered reliably. Reliability wins more repeat orders than a small discount.

25
00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:27.470
Salons, small hotels and event planners want bath bars and gifts, which bring higher margins.

26
00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.560
A laundry business asks Chinyere for regular supply. A single bar is 900 naira.

27
00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:40.000
1 to 4 cartons of 12 are 750 naira per bar.

28
00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:45.040
5 cartons or more are 720 naira per bar.

29
00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:58.730
Her profit is still 137 naira per bar. The laundry orders 5 cartons every two weeks, which is 43,200 naira per order, with almost no selling effort.

30
00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:06.890
To remember. Label honestly, with a batch code. Cost every run fully, and never sell below your cost per bar.

31
00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:19.150
Confirm the money is in your own account before releasing goods, not just a screenshot. And register with CAC and start NAFDAC registration before selling to big retailers.

32
00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:27.070
Now design your labels, cost your own run, and find your first bulk buyer with a sample pack and price ladder.

33
00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.360
Continue with the lessons below.
